+## Sales and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant with a time zone, `qty`
+a whole number) and answers `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 3 }`: the tickets
+imported and the dishes sold on them (the sum of `qty`), leaving out tickets
+that were imported before. If a row is invalid (`bad_request`, 400) or an item
+runs out (`not_enough_stock`, 409), nothing is imported and the message names
+the row; `row 2` is the first data row.
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers a list, in item
+order, for items with any use in those days (inclusive, UTC):
+
+    [{ "itemId": 1, "name": "onion", "unit": "kg", "theoretical": 0.3, "actual": 0.5, "difference": 0.2 }]
+
+`difference` is `actual - theoretical`.
